      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk i feel like the \"innovation\" argument is kinda just a way for them to dodge accountability, u know? like, they use their massive profits to just buy out any small startup that actually has a good idea before they can even compete. do u think that's a valid critique or is it just being anti-business?",
