      "role": "user",
      "content": "right, so if the \"killer acquisition\" thing is a real thing, then it seems like the current laws are basically broken/useless at stopping them. if we don't actually break them up or pass way stricter laws, isn't the whole idea of a \"free market\" just a myth at this point? like, what's the actually realistic solution here?",
