      "content": "If acquisitions are becoming a primary tool for market control, critics argue existing antitrust laws are outdated and ill-equipped to handle modern, digital market dynamics. A realistic set of solutions often debated includes stricter merger review standards, forcing divestitures of certain businesses, or implementing proactive regulations on platform behavior itself. Ultimately, there is a major policy debate about whether the market is truly \"free\" when a few dominant gatekeepers control access to commerce.",
